  "summary": "The Chicago Police Department is auditing officers' potential misuse of outside agencies' license plate reader systems and has proposed policy changes including non-transferable logins, documented law enforcement purpose for each query, monthly audits, and penalties up to prosecution. A draft directive is open for public comment through Nov. 12. The move follows multiple criminal cases against Illinois-area officers accused of misusing Flock data.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The Chicago Police Department is conducting an audit to determine whether cops abused their access to other law enforcement agencies' license plate reader systems.",
      "paragraph_idx": 5
    },
    {
      "quote": "the department said it will make login information for the system non-transferable \u2014 meaning only one department member can use their log-in credentials \u2014 and require that a \"legitimate law enforcement purpose\" be documented for every query",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "On Nov. 12, the Will County Board is set to consider an ordinance to ban automated license plate reader cameras on county property.",
      "paragraph_idx": 14
    }
  ],
